; Each SubViewport update mode, and what it does to a consumer. Every sub-viewport is 32x32 with a red
; left half, sampled by a 100x100 TextureRect. Row 1: DISABLED shows black, ONCE, WHEN_VISIBLE,
; WHEN_PARENT_VISIBLE and ALWAYS show red. Row 2: a DISABLED parent stops its WHEN_PARENT_VISIBLE
; child, and not its WHEN_VISIBLE or ALWAYS ones. Row 3: a ONCE parent renders on frame 1, before a
; WHEN_VISIBLE child has rendered, so it shows black where that child is. An ALWAYS child shows red.
; Right: a SubViewportContainer decides its child's mode (`subviewport_container.cpp:116-128`): a
; hidden one makes it DISABLED, a visible one ALWAYS. Measured with Godot 4.6.3 `--mode 2d`.

[gd_scene format=3]

